<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siege of Vicksburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1863">1863</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Siege of Vicksburg, from May to 4 July 1863, ended with the surrender of the Confederate fortress on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi River</a> in Mississippi to Union forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulysses-s-grant">Ulysses S. Grant</a>. Its fall gave the Union control of the Mississippi and split the Confederacy in two. Coming a day after Gettysburg, it marked a turning point of the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/siege-of-vicksburg.jpg" alt="Siege of Vicksburg" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thure de Thulstrup · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thure_de_Thulstrup_-_Siege_of_Vicksburg_-_Assault_on_Fort_Hill.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
